{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe downward bias: The model consistently overestimates prices by 5-10 EUR when the market is in a downtrend (prices falling from ~65 to ~52), failing to capture the magnitude of the crash.",
    "Eliminate forecast rigidity: The model exhibits excessive inertia, predicting near-flat or slightly rising trajectories regardless of the sharp historical price drops; forecasts must be made more responsive to recent negative momentum.",
    "Adjust for sentiment lag: Despite negative sentiment (-1.00) appearing in the history, the model ignores this signal and maintains a bullish baseline; negative sentiment should trigger an immediate downward adjustment in the forecast baseline.",
    "Reduce overshoot on recovery: The model fails to anticipate the V-shaped recovery (prices rising from ~52 back to ~60) and remains stuck at low levels; forecasts must be more aggressive in capturing mean reversion once the downtrend stabilizes.",
    "Shorten the horizon lag: The model's 30-day forecast is effectively a static extrapolation of the last known price rather than a dynamic projection; reduce the smoothing factor to allow the forecast to track the true outcome's volatility more closely."
  ]
}
